{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca700e0994ad8d52ef83f9809ce11f4ec06e2dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} = \\overline{AC}$\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3219f71c7b21b0d9bc36cc63c9c5800db7c9a481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = 30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e856b98f881b376a9a20614608b053c7ca20c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE} = \\overline{AD}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410ec6ee6021df79d03713b2f7cab84dd3acef06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); pair A=(3,3),B=(0,0),C=(6,0),D=(2,0),E=(5,1); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D--E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NE);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"132\" />\nThe angle CDE equals:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e95222ff6702857398fd8da6f62cf9ec9802f7c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\frac{1}{2}^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 10^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 12\\frac{1}{2}^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 15^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 20^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"448\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faeb50eb18bd11a4e4ba2ee947a7c9db1aec90d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\angle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8873d5e397fa8d1b1a07b7d358b72570b4db224f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAE = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>First, consider the large isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. The vertex angle is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aeb964afe18484873d864ef7d35d11bdc50c72b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAC = \\angle BAD + \\angle DAE = 30^\\circ + a\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since the sum of angles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> and the base angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238db449db9d3160bfe7052f25e799db23f8dfe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> are equal:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248534f99169381a0b4365e293e50399c4bffa42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BCA = \\frac{180^\\circ - (30^\\circ + a)}{2} = 75^\\circ - \\frac{a}{2}\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Next, consider the smaller isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f666e2e651aedf38b50ead09d8bb15cb3871be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. The vertex angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8873d5e397fa8d1b1a07b7d358b72570b4db224f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAE = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />. Since the base angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a009564c26bf86933bd2d32bf0c1b854d12a3084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c66ed16138fe3e47a2002f117b0fde990a48d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> are equal:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97f665a6f338843ee6ae47eef622d24dc4e29c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ADE = \\angle DEA = \\frac{180^\\circ - a}{2} = 90^\\circ - \\frac{a}{2}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now, look at the angles along line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, or by using the exterior angle theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. The exterior angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c66ed16138fe3e47a2002f117b0fde990a48d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to the sum of its two opposite interior angles:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e230e4601b3fbddbb5df193109a1c29290d817a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle DEA = \\angle CDE + \\angle BCA\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Substituting the expressions we found for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c66ed16138fe3e47a2002f117b0fde990a48d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238db449db9d3160bfe7052f25e799db23f8dfe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335d940a1c9ab66fe21ebaae8eea85d978072119.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[90^\\circ - \\frac{a}{2} = x + \\left(75^\\circ - \\frac{a}{2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a92277209c6d113250f5e1f27d86d13e411a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75^\\circ - \\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"34\" /> from both sides gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c15f0e2fa486799d6a9a78c186440b8c7062f6e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 90^\\circ - 75^\\circ = 15^\\circ\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552105d1406b8a19b5d52d8473ecf118df59a5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDE = 15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fb121aa58c9638a0d8268c99d34abf70672a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\